# Files that should not be published as part of the Cloudflare static deploy.
# NOTE: `[assets] directory = "."` makes wrangler walk the whole repo, so the
# repository's own metadata has to be excluded explicitly. Without this, wrangler
# tries to upload .git/objects/pack/*.pack and the deploy fails once that pack
# grows past Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-asset limit.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.assetsignore
wrangler.toml
.github/
docs/
README.txt
.nojekyll
# Internal data-entry templates — never part of the public website.
data-import-kit/

# The build inputs and the build itself. index.html is the deliverable; these
# are how it is made. Published, they hand anyone the commented, unminified
# templates and the tooling — which is both an invitation to clone the site and
# a map of it. Nothing at runtime fetches them: every byte the page needs is
# already inside index.html.
src/
tools/
unrar-0.4-py3-none-any.whl

# A client's own villa, modelled from their dimensioned plans. It belongs in
# the repo, but it is private design work and not part of the public website —
# delete this line if it is ever meant to be served.
villa-3d/
